{"kind":"request","text":"T1 source review found three inherited spike bugs before the final gate at clean 9f9dacf591. All sit within request 00c50371's typed record-element and accurate diagnostic requirements.\n\n1. ElemOf exposes a valid record member named self, but the element Proxy reserves row.self for the complete value. An each guard comparing row.self to 'ready' therefore compares the record instead of its self member. The kernel allows that member name. Preserve whole-element .self and provide a separately named typed helper to read any member (including self), or choose another exact supported escape. A method on the same record would collide with another lawful member name. The agents are preparing the smallest concrete signature; no edit is applied.\n\n2. findings regex-scans quoted rule text. The valid JSONata expression '\"fields.absent\" = \"fields.absent\"' reads no field but compile reports two nonexistent-field reads and refuses. derive/rule currently exposes admit(source):void, while its private compile already uses the pinned JSONata parser and checked AST. We propose a narrow ruleReferences helper on that existing parser, returning direct field/value references for the author package; no second parser, evaluation or raw AST export. Please confirm this small public addition or choose a boundary.\n\n3. The validator emits dotted indices such as acts.establish.effects.0.value.from, but T1's form regex accepts brackets only. A wrong-type value effect prints its operand rather than the offending effect form. This needs a local dotted-boundary correction and an assertion over the complete offending form; it needs no new surface.\n\nThe current focused results remain at their actual checkpoints; these untested paths claim no coverage. We retain the frozen one compile-refusal control at 9f9 and can run it after A releases the single slot, then repair and run only the affected focused owners before the required final gate. Kernel behavior and pins remain unchanged.","body":{"conditions":"Choose the narrow supported T1 list-element escape for a real member named self and approve or amend an existing-parser rule-reference helper for accurate author diagnostics. T1 control/final gate remain pending; no source repair is applied yet.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}